# Festag Projects mobile — Vercel master

`/projects` on ≤768px uses a **Vercel-inspired** home, not the default
`CodexMobileActionPill` + large title + `MobilePageDock` chrome.

Canonical implementation: `components/projects/ProjectsMobileHome.tsx`
(`.pmh-*`). Desktop `/projects` stays on the existing `pj2-*` table.

## Required chrome (do not invent a third pattern)

1. **Top** — centered workspace/app selector (green mark + name + chevron →
   `PortalWorkspacePopover`) and a **grid** button (→ `MobileNavSheet`).
2. **Tools** — search field („Projekte suchen“) + filter square + solid **+**
   (→ `NewProjectModal`).
3. **Recents card** — segmented tabs **Zuletzt / Status / Hinweise**, activity
   rows with avatars + chips, optional expand chevron on the card edge.
4. **Projekte** — section title + bordered **cards** (logo tile, name, host/
   subtitle, status, calm meta line, relative time). No GitHub/deploy noise
   on the client portal.
5. **Floating footer** — compact centered pill **Finden | Menü** (command
   palette + nav sheet). Not the full-width `MobilePageDock` sheet.

## Content rules

- Festag workspace name in the app selector (fallback „Festag“).
- Cards use `live_url` / `staging_url` host when present; otherwise delivery /
  task subtitle — never fake third-party deploy UI.
- Keep client trust: no raw GitHub commits/PRs on this surface.

## Do not

- Reintroduce `MobilePageDock` or `CodexMobileActionPill` on `/projects`
  mobile while this master is active.
- Port Execution-panel GitHub density into the client cards.
- Change desktop `pj2-*` layout while polishing mobile.

When extending this page, match Vercel’s calm density and hierarchy — Festag
labels and data only.
